        "title": {
          "en": "The new classmate"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "A new girl, Kavya, joined the class. She wore a bright blue bag.\n\"Spot the noun, pronoun and adjective,\" said the teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "noun",
          "pronoun",
          "adjective",
          "degrees of comparison"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Nouns name people, places, things and ideas: girl, Chennai, bag and kindness. Proper nouns begin with a capital letter, and collective nouns name groups such as a team or a flock.\nA pronoun replaces a noun: she, they, it. A possessive pronoun shows ownership: mine, yours, hers and theirs. A reflexive pronoun ends in self or selves: herself.\nAn adjective describes a noun: a bright blue bag. Adjectives can compare: tall, taller and tallest."
        }
      },
